/-! # Bounded finite models after polynomial scalar extension

Source: Stacks Project, dualizing.tex, Tag 0BZK, lemma-shriek-boundedness, proof;
more-algebra.tex, Tags 066E and 064K; homology.tex, Tag 0118, canonical truncation.
(blueprint: lem-trf-polynomial-bounded-finite-model).
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

namespace DerivedCategory

/-- Polynomial scalar extension of bounded finite cohomology has a bounded finite module model.
The terms are only required to be finite modules; no perfectness of the input is assumed.
Source: Stacks Project, dualizing.tex, Tag 0BZK, lemma-shriek-boundedness, proof;
more-algebra.tex, Tags 066E and 064K; homology.tex, Tag 0118, canonical truncation.
(blueprint: lem-trf-polynomial-bounded-finite-model).

Proof:
1. Choose cohomology bounds l <= t. By
   lem-weil-pbc-noetherian-pseudocoherent-cohomology-criterion (066E), K is pseudo-coherent.
   Unpack def-pc-ring-pseudo-coherent-complex to choose a bounded-above finite free R-complex F,
   zero above v, and e : Q(F) isomorphic to K.
2. Finite free modules are flat, since their tensor functors are finite direct sums.
   By lem-pc-module-bounded-flat-kflat, F is K-flat. Apply lem-pur-derived-change-of-rings
   to the identity K-flat resolution of F. For E = F tensor_R P, its counit gives
   c : L(Q(F)) isomorphic to Q(E), where L is derived scalar extension. Thus
   h = c.symm followed by L(e) identifies Q(E) with L(K). Each E^i is finite free:
   the maps R^r tensor_R P to P^r and back send z tensor p to (z_s p)_s and
   (p_s)_s to the sum of e_s tensor p_s. Also E vanishes above v.
3. By def-weil-pbc-mv-polynomial-ring, monomials give an R-basis of P. Coefficient maps
   identify E, as an R-complex, with the direct sum of copies of F indexed by monomials.
   Cycles and boundaries are coordinatewise; boundary preimages can be chosen on the finite
   support. Consequently its cohomology is the corresponding direct sum of H^i(F), and
   vanishes below l (and above t).
4. Set a = l and b = max l v. Truncate E below a, with G^a the cokernel of d_E^{a-1},
   zero terms below a, and E^i above a. The differential descends since d squared is zero.
   The projection p : E to G is a chain map. In degree a its cohomology is
   ker(d_E^a)/im(d_E^{a-1}); in degree a+1 the incoming differential has the same image
   as d_E^a; above that the differentials are unchanged. Below a both cohomologies vanish.
   Hence p is a quasi-isomorphism. The bottom term is generated by images of a finite basis,
   and all other terms are finite free or zero (def-weil-finitely-generated-module).
   Thus G is zero outside [a,b] with finite P-terms. By def-weil-abstract-derived-category,
   localization inverts p; Q(p).symm followed by h is the required isomorphism. -/
theorem exists_bounded_finite_model_polynomial_scalarExtension
    (R : Type u) [CommRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R] (n : ℕ)
    (K : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} R))
    (_hbounded : ∃ l t : ℤ, l ≤ t ∧ ∀ i : ℤ,
      i < l ∨ t < i → IsZero ((homologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) i).obj K))
    (_hfinite : ∀ i : ℤ, Module.Finite R ((homologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) i).obj K)) :
    ∃ (a b : ℤ) (G : CochainComplex (ModuleCat.{u} (MvPolynomial (Fin n) R)) ℤ),
      a ≤ b ∧ (∀ j : ℤ, j < a ∨ b < j → IsZero (G.X j)) ∧
        (∀ j : ℤ, Module.Finite (MvPolynomial (Fin n) R) (G.X j)) ∧
        Nonempty (Q.obj G ≅
          (ModuleCat.ordinaryDerivedExtendScalars
            (MvPolynomial.C : R →+* MvPolynomial (Fin n) R)).obj K) := by
  sorry

end DerivedCategory
